Reports terrain at exactly 0 m under the map center, and only ground that a
loaded DEM tile covers. The renderer started from a last reported height of
0 m, so it never reported sea-level ground, and a clamped center over it never
learned of the ground: the clamp neither settled the center there nor lifted an
eye under a cliff beside the sea. And it read the center's height where
getElevationForLatLng answers 0 m without a DEM tile, so a clamped center moved
onto ground still loading dropped toward sea level until the tile arrived. The
height now starts unknown, and every report waits for a loaded DEM tile under
the center, as the animation target's already does. findElevationForLatLng
finds the covering DEM tile and samples it in one search, so a frame reads the
center's height with the same two passes over the DEM tiles as before.
Upstream: not proposed

